    This study has the following objectives:

1. Design a mobile-based application with the following features:
   • A GPS-enabled interface that displays nearby mechanics based on the user's real-time location;
   • A mechanic profile system containing ratings, service offerings, availability status, and contact information;
   • A booking and transaction module for scheduled and emergency repair requests;
   • An in-app review and rating system to ensure service credibility;
   • A price comparison feature that allows users to compare service rates among mechanics and repair shops; and
   • An emergency assessment and checklist feature that enables users to identify possible vehicle issues and communicate relevant information to mechanics before service dispatch.
2. Develop the system using React Native, Supabase, and Google Maps API integration.
3. Test and improve the application in terms of usability, performance efficiency, functionality, and system responsiveness.
4. Evaluate the functionality, reliability, usability, performance efficiency, security, maintainability, and portability of the developed system using the ISO/IEC 25010 software quality standards.
